{# The Work Log guide (1.0.0), mailed in the welcome email to everyone with
   an account. Inline styles, because it is mailed; page_url is absolute. #}
<h3 style="margin:16px 0 6px;font-size:16px;">What it is for</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
    A place to jot down what you just did, in a few seconds, and find it again
    later: for your own memory, or when you write up your week. Tasks are for
    what is still to do; the Work Log is for what is done.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:16px 0 6px;font-size:16px;">Logging something</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
    Three ways in, all the same box: <strong>Log what I just did</strong> under
    the <strong>+</strong> at the top of every page, the <strong>Today's log</strong>
    box on your dashboard, and the top of <a href="{{ page_url }}">My log</a>.
    Type a line and press <strong>Enter</strong>. It is timed now; for something
    from earlier, pick the date and time in <strong>When</strong>. Tick a task
    done on your list and it is logged here too, as
    &ldquo;[Task Completed] &hellip;&rdquo;.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:16px 0 6px;font-size:16px;">Finding it again</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
    <a href="{{ page_url }}">My log</a> lists everything, newest day first.
    Type in its search box to narrow it: every word you type has to appear, and
    a phrase in quotes is matched exactly. Click <strong>When</strong> to turn
    the order around.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:16px 0 6px;font-size:16px;">Changing or removing an entry</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
    Each entry on My log has a <strong>&hellip;</strong> menu: <strong>Edit</strong>
    changes its words or its time, and <strong>Delete</strong> removes it after
    asking.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:16px 0 6px;font-size:16px;">Taking it with you</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
    At the bottom of My log, pick the dates (this week, to start with) and
    choose <strong>Word</strong> or <strong>CSV</strong>.
</p>

<h3 style="margin:16px 0 6px;font-size:16px;">Who can see it</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
    Only you. Nobody else can open it from their own account on the intranet
    &mdash; your supervisor and the site's administrators included.
</p>
